  "worked_solution": "First, we calculate the second derivative of $f(x),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(x) & =2x-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2} \\\\ {f}^{\u2033}(x) & =2-x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find where the function is concave up, we need to solve ${f}^{\u2033}(x)>0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2-x & >0\\,\u27f9\\,x<2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the function is concave up on $(-\\infty ,2).$\n\nThe function $f(x)$ is concave down when ${f}^{\u2033}(x)<0.$ By similar reasoning to before, this leads to the inequality $2-x<0,$ which has the solution $(2,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"",
